# {{ProjectName}} — Project Memory

A fast, **layered REST API** in Node.js — **plain JavaScript (ESM), functional style, no classes, no
TypeScript**. Architecture rules are authoritative: see the `architecture-rules` skill
(node-pg-express plugin).

## This project
- Server: Express 5, single process, one file-based router built at startup.
- Layers (strict one-way `api -> services -> data`, `lib` shared by all):
  - `src/api/` — file-based routes, folder-per-method (`customers/get/route.js` -> GET /customers;
    `[id]` -> `:id`). `route.js` default-exports the handler; a sibling `schema.json` (JSON Schema)
    validates input.
  - `src/services/` — business logic, HTTP-agnostic plain functions.
  - `src/data/` — repositories; the only place that touches Postgres, via one `pg` Pool.
  - `src/lib/` — config, logger (Winston: console + rolling file), errors, asyncHandler,
    respond (envelope), validate (Ajv), auth, rate-limit, idempotency, query-params.
- Database: PostgreSQL via raw `pg` (no ORM). `DATABASE_URL` in `.env`.
- Validation: JSON Schema via Ajv — one library, used for both request input (`schema.json`) and env
  (`config.js`). No Zod. Clean data on `req.valid.{headers,params,query,body}`.
- Imports: Node-native `#/` alias (package.json `"imports": { "#/*": "./src/*" }`) —
  `import x from '#/lib/x.js'`, never relative `../../..`.
- Cross-cutting: auth (global x-api-key + public allowlist) and rate limit (global) are wired in
  `app.js`; idempotency is opt-in per route (`export const middleware = [idempotency]`). Responses use
  the `res.ok`/`res.created`/`res.page` envelope (`{ data, links|pagination, message }`).
- Resources so far: {{ResourceList}}

## Non-negotiables
- Plain JS, ESM, functional — NO classes. Runtime validation with Zod at the API edge.
- Routes are thin: validate input, call ONE service, shape the response. No SQL in `src/api/`.
- Services never import `express` / touch `req`/`res`; they take plain args, return plain data,
  throw the `lib/errors.js` factories.
- Only repositories talk to Postgres, via `pool` — parameterized queries only, multi-statement
  writes through `withTransaction`.
- Add a resource (route + service + repository) with the `new-resource` skill; for each concern see
  the `request-validation`, `auth`, `rate-limiting`, `idempotency`, `list-queries`, `responses` skills.
